#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176641} :activity/id #uuid "a99096db-e777-5aa5-ab89-cb129fc1fb0f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048282 :topic/id #uuid "901a2659-6453-5c9f-bdff-c073380fe867" :topic/math-academy-id 3576} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176641 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176949 :tutorial/content "The **total displacement** $d$ of a particle over the time interval $t \\in [a,b]$ is the difference in the position of the particle between $t=a$ and $t=b.$\n\n$$\nd = x(b) - x(a).\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental theorem of calculus states that\n\n$$\nd = x(b) - x(a) = \\int_a^b x'(t) \\, \\textrm dt\n$$\n\nand since $x'(t) = v(t),$ we can find the total displacement of a particle by integrating the velocity:\n\n$$\nd = x(b) - x(a) = \\int_a^b v(t) \\, \\textrm dt\n$$\n\nTo summarize, the total displacement of a particle over the time interval $t \\in [a,b]$ can be found by integrating the velocity $v(t)$ over the time interval $t\\in[a,b].$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "eaade9c6-bf5a-51de-b56f-538581c3c761" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1018 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6be48168-ab6c-55cf-8322-297a1c8e496f" :step/math-academy-id 2000 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176642}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176642 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175927 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175786 :question/id #uuid "f2597771-4f5e-5a90-9c39-d8b902690340" :question/math-academy-id "e-568"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7ca7dee-1a1b-5af6-8719-5d2377004be9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050819}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176433} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176434} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256497} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287950} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290528} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319241} {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218632083